 "drivingQuestion": "With what do they sound the alarm on the last seven fasts?",
 "outcome": "inconclusive",
 "outcomeNote": "two views recorded, no decision in this unit",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "taanit.14a.7",
   "daf": "14a",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "מָה אֵלּוּ יְתֵירוֹת עַל הָרִאשׁוֹנוֹת, אֶלָּא שֶׁבְּאֵלּוּ מַתְרִיעִין וְנוֹעֲלִין אֶת הַחֲנוּיוֹת. בְּמַאי מַתְרִיעִין? רַב יְהוּדָה אָמַר: בְּשׁוֹפָרוֹת, וְרַב יְהוּדָה בְּרֵיהּ דְּרַב שְׁמוּאֵל בַּר שִׁילַת מִשְּׁמֵיהּ דְּרַב אָמַר: בַּ״עֲנֵנוּ״.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «How are these» seven fast days «more» stringent «than the first ones? Rather,» the difference is «that on these» days, in addition to all the earlier stringencies, «they sound the alarm and they lock the stores.» The Gemara asks: «With what do they sound the alarm? Rav Yehuda said: With shofarot. And Rav Yehuda, son of Rav Shmuel bar Sheilat, said in the name of Rav: With» the «Aneinu» prayer."
  }
 ],
